From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8996: keep the PCIe GDSCs on in system suspend

The qcom PCIe driver keeps the link of a controller with an active device
up across system suspend (qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq). genpd still powers off
the controller's GDSC in the noirq phase once its devices are suspended,
which takes the link and the device down underneath the driver. On the
Mi MIX (QCA6174 Wi-Fi on PCIe0) every s2idle attempt, and pm_test at the
platform level, resets the phone; without the Wi-Fi device it passes.

Mark the PCIe GDSCs PWRSTS_RET_ON, as done for other Qualcomm SoCs, so
genpd leaves them on and the hardware handles retention.

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
@@ -3239,7 +3239,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie0",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie1_gdsc = {
@@ -3247,7 +3247,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie1",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie2_gdsc = {
@@ -3255,7 +3255,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie2",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc ufs_gdsc = {
